{"id":"louvre-museum","name":"Louvre Museum","qid":"Q19675","country":"France","locality":"Saint-Germain-l'Auxerrois","lat":"48.861111111","lon":"2.335833333","built":"1793","year":1793,"year_text":"1793","century":"18th century","era":"Early modern","period":"","date_basis":"Wikidata, inception","style":"","heritage":"","type":"art museum; archaeological museum","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louvre","text":"The Louvre (French: Musée du Louvre [myze dy luvʁ] ) is a national art museum in Paris, France. It is located on the Right Bank of the Seine in the city's 1st arrondissement (district) and home to some of the most canonical works of Western art, including the Mona Lisa, Venus de Milo, and Winged Victory. The museum is housed in the Louvre Palace, originally built in the late 12th to 13th century under Philip II.","text_source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louvre","text_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","real":[{"id":"gh-288b47311778","w":1200,"h":476,"title":"Cour Napoléon at night - Louvre.jpg","o":"gh-288b47311778.jpg","credit":{"text":"Benh LIEU SONG","license":"CC BY 2.5","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.5","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cour_Napol%C3%A9on_at_night_-_Louvre.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}},{"id":"gh-8149dfddca18","w":1200,"h":800,"title":"Louvre Paris from top.jpg","o":"gh-8149dfddca18.jpg","credit":{"text":"Matthias Kabel","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","license_url":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Louvre_Paris_from_top.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}}],"depictions":[{"id":"civilization-v--louvre","game":"civilization-v","name":"Louvre","verified":false,"text":"The is a wonder in the Civilization games.","text_source":"https://civilization.fandom.com/wiki/Louvre","text_license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","images":[{"id":"gh-p6a45bcefad7","w":972,"h":568,"o":"gh-p6a45bcefad7.png","credit":{"text":"Screenshot from Civilization V, © 2K; Aspyr.","so